00:09:06.185 --> 00:09:07.018
- And doing something more normal.

00:09:07.018 --> 00:09:09.870
- And just seeing another world and not,

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.840
and being a kid,

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.610
the having that sort of experience.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.220
And then I also wanted to win,

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.053
do you know what I mean?

00:09:18.053 --> 00:09:19.860
I wanted to prove to other people,

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:22.665
but to myself, that you can't,

00:09:22.665 --> 00:09:26.370
I'm right here and I have
grown into this person

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.540
and I'm like a weevil,

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.949
you're not gonna knock me over.

00:09:28.949 --> 00:09:30.750
I'm gonna come right back.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.159
- I love that.

00:09:32.159 --> 00:09:33.222
(audience applauding)

00:09:33.222 --> 00:09:34.055
You had success very early on

00:09:34.055 --> 00:09:35.460
but then you said you went to college.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.620
So like, after that,
like after you graduated

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.270
what was it like, getting back in,

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.170
it was harder right?

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.070
- Oh, huh.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:41.903
I was-

00:09:41.903 --> 00:09:42.736
- She said, "Oh huh."

00:09:42.736 --> 00:09:45.600
- So known non grata.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.210
I was so shocked

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.060
because basically the
entire industry was like,

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.686
oh no, we're good.

00:09:52.686 --> 00:09:55.053
We, you've been away,

00:09:56.066 --> 00:09:58.140
and then in that, in the interim,

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:02.460
a whole new crop of young
actresses and actors

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.293
sort of came up

00:10:03.293 --> 00:10:05.490
and they were the hot thing.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.667
And I had gained weight in college

00:10:08.667 --> 00:10:11.550
and I was sort of in this stage

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:12.750
where I was a bit awkward

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.990
and it just, I couldn't get a job.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.830
I mean, I literally ended up
having to do weird commercials

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.540
in other languages in other countries

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.620
just to pay the bills.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.910
And it was such a shock
but I ended up studying.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.140
I just started studying.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.990
I started dancing, I started taking class

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:32.640
I started studying acting,

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:34.110
which I'd never done before.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:34.943
- Yeah.

00:10:34.943 --> 00:10:38.370
- And one of my first
jobs back was Broadway,

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.610
was "Grease", on Broadway.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:42.443
And then-

00:10:42.443 --> 00:10:43.320
- Being on stage is,

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.260
for me, I love being
on stage in that sense

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:48.420
the live aspect of like,
going straight through.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:49.380
And I love that feeling.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.460
I think that energy is so cool.

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.480
- And you can find, I mean

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.970
I've done shows for six
months, a year at a time.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.650
And you can find something.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.420
You do the same shows, same blocking.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.253
- But it's different.

00:10:58.253 --> 00:10:59.766
- [Brooke] Different every night.

00:10:59.766 --> 00:11:00.610
- I know yeah.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:01.890
- So it was just fun.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.870
And it was fun to be a part of a company.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.190
So I came out of college-

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.023
- It's like a family.

00:11:06.023 --> 00:11:07.313
- And, yeah very much.

00:11:07.313 --> 00:11:09.060
I mean, but I came out of college

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.890
and nobody really wanted to hire me.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:14.220
And it was very difficult ego wise

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:15.723
it was very difficult,

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.810
bill wise paying keeping up,

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.190
by then my mom was just,

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:22.560
she just like bought houses
every time we made movies

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.460
she'd buy a house.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:27.270
And we had all this
property and no capital.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:28.140
And it was,

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.540
it was a real shock and I just thought,

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.340
okay, I'm gonna have to start.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.510
What am I gonna do now?

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.040
And we had no plan.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.870
We just needed to buy a car.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.150
So I would do this movie or whatever,

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:41.700
there was no real thought process.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.620
- One thing I also love about you,

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.570
because I have a lot of friends

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.640
that have suffered from
postpartum depression

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.100
and people don't understand it

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.780
if you've never experienced it, right.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.460
Like, even them describing to me,

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.410
like I never really quite,

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:57.240
you can't get what someone's feeling.

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:00.660
And I love how not only
you were open about it

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.060
but then people came against you about it

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.500
and you ended up writing
the op-ed about it.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.360
I think that that is so important

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.400
and I know it's not easy to do,

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.510
like you said it's not easy to do

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:10.500
when you're an actress in the public

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:11.520
or anybody in the public eye.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:12.690
People are like, just shut up and sing,

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.010
or shut up and act like you know,

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:14.843
they don't want you to

00:12:14.843 --> 00:12:16.230
have an opinion about anything.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:18.690
And even though you're human in a society

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:19.770
and living with everybody else,

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:21.870
but it was so, it's so important

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.330
because not a lot of people
have a voice for that.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.010
And you have a giant spotlight on you.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.930
So for you to not only
stand up for yourself,

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.910
but stand up for all those other women,

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:30.840
it was incredible.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.658
And it's like one of my favorite
things you've ever done.

00:12:32.658 --> 00:12:33.904
(audience applauding)

00:12:33.904 --> 00:12:37.170
And it just takes, it takes a lot of guts

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.610
to do something like that and bravery,

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.470
is it, was it easy for you to...

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.480
Do you do well in situations like that?

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.313
You know what I'm saying?

00:12:43.313 --> 00:12:45.180
- I think writing a book is a very

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.390
introverted sort of action.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.100
You sort of, you really do have to sit

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.360
with you, your thoughts

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.430
and really kind of be willing to go there.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.243
So that was a very
comfortable endeavor for me.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:01.080
Telling the story it didn't feel,

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:02.880
I don't know if it was courageous,

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.650
but it was necessary.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:08.280
And I think that as a mother of a daughter

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.560
at the time now two daughters,

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.140
I owe it to them to be,

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.330
to tell the truth about something

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:17.610
that is so frightening.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.740
So many people suffer,

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.770
untreated it can be devastating.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:24.420
And really just to say,

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.280
I don't wanna feel alone.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.620
I can't be the only one feeling this.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.667
- Yeah.

00:13:29.667 --> 00:13:31.110
- Please and I was a plea as well

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:32.854
for people to, for,

00:13:32.854 --> 00:13:35.460
to learn that I wasn't alone.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.150
And that, and the power in
being able to ask for help

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.220
and there's no shame in it.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.410
And I think that's not the way, I grew up

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.450
you just stiff upper lip and you just,

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.220
show must go on and that's what you do.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.566
And this undid me.

00:13:49.566 --> 00:13:52.260
And when I started doing research on it,

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.360
I thought someone's gotta tell this story

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.360
because people and families are suffering.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.710
- Yeah.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:02.040
- The people around who love
the person going through it

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.960
they don't know what to do.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.100
They don't know how to fix it

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:07.230
because it doesn't and it's custom made.

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.410
It is custom made to each person.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.400
And it's brilliant

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.350
because it answers all
the negative questions

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:16.690
and they all, it is an
imbalance, it's biochemical

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:20.370
and you feel that that word crazy

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.200
keeps being floated around you

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.480
and you just keep thinking
what's wrong with me?

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.700
People have been having
babies since the dawn of time

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.010
and they gaze down at their infant

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.570
and their hair cascades

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.190
and the baby looks up and,

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:33.036
all's well with the world.

00:14:33.036 --> 00:14:33.869
- Angel are singing.

00:14:33.869 --> 00:14:34.702
- Angels are singing.

00:14:34.702 --> 00:14:35.618
- And everything's perfect.

00:14:35.618 --> 00:14:38.430
- And it's just, it's a lot harder.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:41.160
And I just wanted to be
able to be honest about it

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:44.130
because I knew nobody
was talking about this

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.710
and I thought I refused
to find shame in this.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:48.390
I need to get through this.

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:49.470
- I love that you say it's like a plea

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.000
and like reaching out as well.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:51.833
- [Brooke] Absolutely.

00:14:51.833 --> 00:14:53.250
- That's what living is about connecting,

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.720
I think and relationships

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.283
- And making it okay.

00:14:56.283 --> 00:14:57.287
- [Kelly] Those bigger conversations.

00:14:57.287 --> 00:14:58.380
- And again, it's tough

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:01.410
but it's, you can get through these things

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.818
and ask for help, you know?

00:15:02.818 --> 00:15:03.704
- Absolutely.

00:15:03.704 --> 00:15:04.537
(audience applauding)

